# Built output. Both files are deterministic functions of the committed sources:
#
#   node scripts/embed-assets.mjs   src/assets.js   <- assets/*.jpg + assets/lightness.json
#   node scripts/build.mjs          lib/            <- src/
#
# `lib/client.js` is a single file carrying every artwork as base64, so it is large and
# changes on every art edit. Committing it would put a 3.8 MB blob in the history for each
# image tweak, and it rebuilds byte-for-byte from what is already here.
#
# `scripts/prepare-assets.py` is NOT needed for that: it only turns the original PNG
# masters (which are not in this repo) into assets/*.jpg, and those are committed.
lib/
src/assets.js
